<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--

InoOnnx — Unreal Plugin Language (UPL) file for Android APK packaging
of the ONNX Runtime shared library.

Referenced from InoOnnx.Build.cs via
    AdditionalPropertiesForReceipt.Add("AndroidPlugin", "<this file>")

Two concerns handled here, matching the proven pattern from the
sibling InoLiteRT plugin's InoLiteRT_UPL_Android.xml:

  1. Java-side loadLibrary: emit System.loadLibrary("InoOnnxRuntime")
     in the generated GameActivity Java so the library is loaded
     before libUnreal.so runs.

  2. APK staging: copy libInoOnnxRuntime.so from the plugin's
     Source/ThirdParty/Android/arm64-v8a/ into the APK's
     lib/arm64-v8a/ directory so Android's dynamic linker can find
     it via dlopen() at runtime.

Both are required. Empirically, Build.cs RuntimeDependencies alone
does NOT stage a .so into lib/arm64-v8a/ of the APK — explicit
<copyFile> in <resourceCopies> is what gets it there.

Path variable gotchas (lessons from the LiteRT-LM UPL):

  $S(AbsPluginDir)  — resolves to THIS MODULE's directory, i.e.
                       Plugins/InoOnnx/Source/InoOnnx/
                       (despite the "Plugin" in the name — that's how
                       UE's UPL engine labels it).
  $S(PluginDir)     — does NOT exist as a UPL variable; using it
                       produces an empty string and silently breaks the
                       copy. Always use $S(AbsPluginDir).
  $S(BuildDir)      — Intermediate/Android/<arch>/gradle/app/src/main/
  $S(Architecture)  — arm64-v8a, etc.

Our .so lives at
    Plugins/InoOnnx/Source/ThirdParty/Android/arm64-v8a/libInoOnnxRuntime.so
which is one level up from $S(AbsPluginDir), then down through ThirdParty.

Docs: https://docs.unrealengine.com/en-US/Sharing/Reference/UnrealPluginLanguage/

-->
<root xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

	<!-- File trace for debugging: UE logs a line whenever this UPL is
	     processed. Useful for confirming the packager picked it up. -->
	<trace enable="true"/>

	<!--
	init: runs once per architecture. Gate the copies on architecture so
	we don't try to copy arm64-v8a binaries into a different arch's build
	dir. Matches the stock UE UPL pattern (see e.g. Engine/Source/ThirdParty/
	libGPUCounters/libGPUCounters_UPL.xml).
	-->
	<init>
		<log text="InoOnnx UPL init"/>
		<setBool result="bSupported" value="false"/>
		<isArch arch="arm64-v8a">
			<setBool result="bSupported" value="true"/>
		</isArch>
		<if condition="bSupported">
			<false>
				<log text="InoOnnx: unsupported architecture $S(Architecture), skipping ORT staging"/>
			</false>
		</if>
	</init>

	<!--
	soLoadLibrary: emit System.loadLibrary("InoOnnxRuntime") in the
	Java launcher activity so the ORT .so is resident by the time
	InoOnnxModule::Init's dlopen call runs.

	Since we no longer PublicAdditionalLibraries on Android, libUnreal.so
	does NOT DT_NEEDED our library — the dynamic linker wouldn't pick
	it up automatically. The soLoadLibrary preload here is what gets
	it mapped into the process. If it fails we get a catchable Java
	UnsatisfiedLinkError rather than a silent native abort.

	Named "InoOnnxRuntime" to match the renamed .so file
	(libInoOnnxRuntime.so, Android convention lib<name>.so →
	System.loadLibrary("<name>")).

	failmsg surfaces in logcat as
	    "AndroidJNI failed to load library 'InoOnnxRuntime'. Reason: <failmsg>"
	-->
	<soLoadLibrary>
		<loadLibrary name="InoOnnxRuntime" failmsg="Failed to load libInoOnnxRuntime.so — ensure OnnxRuntime/scripts/setup-onnxruntime.ps1 has been run and the APK re-packaged."/>
	</soLoadLibrary>

	<!--
	resourceCopies: copy libInoOnnxRuntime.so (our renamed ORT runtime)
	into the APK's lib/arm64-v8a/ directory. The rename to a unique
	filename lets our .so coexist in the same APK with any marketplace
	plugin's libonnxruntime.so — which would otherwise be a filename
	collision in the lib/<arch>/ directory, and the last-writer would
	clobber the other.
	-->
	<resourceCopies>
		<if condition="bSupported">
			<true>
				<copyFile
					src="$S(AbsPluginDir)/../ThirdParty/Android/$S(Architecture)/libInoOnnxRuntime.so"
					dst="$S(BuildDir)/libs/$S(Architecture)/libInoOnnxRuntime.so"/>
				<log text="InoOnnx: copied libInoOnnxRuntime.so"/>
			</true>
		</if>
	</resourceCopies>

</root>
